index 0ece82591..4066d2c9d 100644
--- a/docs/README-ps4.md
+++ b/docs/README-ps4.md
@@ -19,8 +19,33 @@ With the SDK installed (`PS4_HOMEBREW_SDK`, by default `/opt/ps4-homebrew-sdk`):
    ${MAKE} -C build install DESTDIR="${SYSROOT}"
 ```
 SDL is a static library; link it with `orbis-pkg-config --libs sdl2`, which
-adds the system libraries it calls (libScePad, libSceUserService,
-libSceSystemService and libSceSysmodule).
+adds SDL2main and the system libraries SDL calls (libScePad,
+libSceUserService, libSceSystemService, libSceSysmodule and
+libSceAppContent).
+
+SDL2main
+--------
+SDL2main provides `main()` (the program's `main()` becomes `SDL_main()`,
+see `SDL_main.h`). Before the program starts it sets up the XDG base
+directories, unless they are set already:
+
+| Variable          | Folder                                                  |
+|-------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
+| `XDG_CACHE_HOME`  | `.cache` in the folder below                            |
+| `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` | `.config`                                               |
+| `XDG_DATA_HOME`   | `.data`                                                 |
+| `XDG_STATE_HOME`  | `.state`                                                |
+
+The folder is `/temp0`, the title's temporary data, when it can be mounted
+(libSceAppContent only mounts it for a game application, category `gd`);
+otherwise it is `common_temp` in the sandbox, which all homebrew share.
+`/data` is not always mounted, so SDL does not use it.
+
+When the program is finished, SDL2main exits back to the home screen with
+`sceSystemServiceLoadExec("exit", NULL)`.
+
+With `SDL_MAIN_HANDLED`, or without SDL2main, the program sets up the XDG
+base directories itself.
 
